// The Default universe for the Open Universe - one authored file holding the
// whole world: identity (the level-1 heading), its clans, the generic clan jobs
// they offer, and the shared narrative arcs. This is the primary way to build a
// universe (see UNIVERSE_CHANGES.md capstone). Heading level sets structure:
//   #   the universe (identity + future tuning knobs)
//   ##  a section: Clans / Jobs / Narrative
//   ### an entry within a section (a clan, a job type, a narrative step)
// Each heading's `---` data fence carries its YAML. Data fence is a line of only
// dashes. Loaded by universe_clans.py / universe_clan_quests.py.

# [Default](default)
---
display: Default
---
A living frontier of clans, trade, reputation, and contestable space docks. The
galaxy reacts to who you are, not to a scripted hero.

## [Clans](clans)

The factions that hold this galaxy. Each heading key is the clan's side key; the
data section sets identity + home systems; the prose is the description. Spawned
as sides by universe_clans.py.

makeup = the race composition of a clan's ships: a single race ("Torgoth"), an
even list ([Torgoth, Kralien]), or a weighted dict ({Torgoth: 70, Kralien: 30}).
Omit it for a random mix. Races: Kralien, Torgoth, Arvonian, Ximni.

### [Iron Concord](iron)
---
color: "#3399ff"
archetype: military
diplomacy: neutral
homes: [[6, 4]]
leans: { by_the_book: 40, fearsome: 30, honest: 20 }
quest_pool: [patrol, escort, strike]
makeup: { Kralien: 60, Arvonian: 40 }
---
Disciplined and territorial. Respects strength and straight dealing; honor a deal
and the Concord remembers - break one and they remember longer.

### [Verdant Pact](verdant)
---
color: "#44cc88"
archetype: trader
diplomacy: neutral
homes: [[-5, 3]]
leans: { peaceful: 40, generous: 30, kind: 20 }
quest_pool: [supply, escort, survey]
makeup: [Arvonian]
---
Green-world traders and farmers. Quick to deal, slow to fight; pay them in
kindness and they pay you back in goods.

### [Free Holders](free)
---
color: "#bb8855"
archetype: settler
diplomacy: neutral
homes: [[-7, -7]]
leans: { resourceful: 40, honest: 30, kind: 10 }
quest_pool: [salvage, rescue, supply]
makeup: [Kralien, Torgoth, Arvonian, Ximni]
---
Independent settlers scratching a living from the drift. Self-reliant and plain-
spoken; they value a captain who gets things done.

### [Mercury Guild](mercury)
---
color: "#ffbb00"
archetype: mercenary
diplomacy: neutral
homes: [[5, -3]]
leans: { resourceful: 30, selfish: 30, fearsome: 20 }
quest_pool: [bounty, escort, smuggle]
makeup: { Ximni: 40, Torgoth: 30, Kralien: 30 }
---
Brokers of muscle and cargo - loyal to the contract, not the cause. Coin and a
fearsome reputation open their doors.

### [Ashfang Raiders](ashfang)
---
color: "#ee3333"
archetype: pirate
diplomacy: foe
homes: [[8, -5]]
leans: { violent: 40, cruel: 30, cowardly: 20 }
quest_pool: [raid, smuggle, bounty]
makeup: [Torgoth]
---
Opportunist pirates who prey on the lanes. They respect violence and despise the
weak; only the dangerous bargain with them.

### [Hollow Choir](choir)
---
color: "#9933ff"
archetype: cult
diplomacy: foe
homes: [[-4, 6]]
leans: { intellectual: 40, liar: 30, selfish: 20 }
quest_pool: [retrieve, escort, mystery]
makeup: [Ximni]
---
A secretive cult chasing forbidden knowledge in the deep dark. Honeyed words hide
sharp intent; trust them at your peril.

## [Jobs](jobs)

Generic clan jobs. Each heading key IS a pool type (see a clan's quest_pool); a
clan offers the jobs whose type is in its pool, gated + reward-scaled by the
captain's standing (universe_clan_quests.py). data: tier (1 basic / 2 / 3
premium), objective, an on_* trigger, base reward. Authoring stays open - a clan
may later carry its own bespoke quests; this is the shared baseline.

### [Patrol Sweep](patrol)
---
tier: 1
objective: Destroy 4 raiders
on_kill: { role: raider, count: 4 }
reward: { credits: 300 }
---
Raiders have been probing our space. Sweep the system and drive them off.

### [Standing Bounty](bounty)
---
tier: 1
objective: Destroy 3 raiders
on_kill: { role: raider, count: 3 }
reward: { credits: 280 }
---
There is a price on raider hulls. Collect three and the bounty is yours.

### [Supply Run](supply)
---
tier: 1
objective: Recover 3 crates of provisions
on_collect: { key: provisions, count: 3 }
reward: { credits: 260 }
---
Our stores are thin. Gather provision crates adrift in the system and bring
them in.

### [Survey Contract](survey)
---
tier: 1
objective: Scan 2 derelicts
on_scan: { role: universe_derelict, count: 2 }
reward: { credits: 300 }
---
We need eyes on the wrecks out here. Scan the derelicts and report what you find.

### [Salvage Sweep](salvage)
---
tier: 1
objective: Recover 2 tech components
on_collect: { key: tech, count: 2 }
reward: { credits: 340 }
---
There is working tech in the debris if you know where to look. Bring it back and
we will make it worth your while.

### [Convoy Escort](escort)
---
tier: 1
objective: Dock at a station
on_dock: { role: station, count: 1 }
reward: { credits: 260 }
---
See our cargo safely to port. Dock at a station and the contract is fulfilled.

### [Run the Lanes](smuggle)
---
tier: 2
objective: Recover 2 contraband caches
on_collect: { key: contraband, count: 2 }
reward: { credits: 480 }
---
Quiet cargo, quiet questions. Recover the caches and keep this between us.

### [Raid the Lanes](raid)
---
tier: 2
objective: Destroy 5 raiders
on_kill: { role: raider, count: 5 }
reward: { credits: 500 }
---
Hit them before they hit us. Five hulls, and do not be gentle about it.

### [Retrieve the Cache](retrieve)
---
tier: 2
objective: Recover 3 tech components
on_collect: { key: tech, count: 3 }
reward: { credits: 520 }
---
Something we want is scattered in the drift. Retrieve three components - discreetly.

### [Search and Rescue](rescue)
---
tier: 2
objective: Scan a derelict, then dock
on_scan: { role: universe_derelict, count: 1 }
reward: { credits: 460 }
---
A ship went dark out here. Find the wreck, recover what survives, and bring it home.

### [Strike Package](strike)
---
tier: 3
objective: Destroy 8 raiders
on_kill: { role: raider, count: 8 }
reward: { credits: 760 }
---
We are done waiting. Take the fight to them - eight hulls, and break their nerve.

### [Chase the Whisper](mystery)
---
tier: 3
objective: Scan 3 derelicts
on_scan: { role: universe_derelict, count: 3 }
reward: { credits: 720 }
---
The signs are out there for those who would read them. Scan the wrecks. Tell no
one what you see.

## [Narrative](narrative)

Shared story arcs - game-wide reveal chains spanning systems, reusing the quest
trigger vocab. Each heading is one step; data sets scope (shared), starting state
(active now / secret = revealed later), the trigger, the next step to reveal, and
rewards. Granted at universe start via quest_grant_amd (universe.mast).

### [The Long Truce: Summons](truce_1)
---
scope: shared
state: active
on_reach: { sector: [6, 4] }
reveal: truce_2
---
A coded hail from Iron Concord HQ at system (6, 4). Travel there to hear them out.

### [The Long Truce: Proof of Resolve](truce_2)
---
scope: shared
state: secret
on_kill: { role: ashfang, count: 3 }
reveal: truce_3
reward: { credits: 100 }
---
The Concord wants a broker for a ceasefire with the Ashfang Raiders. Thin the
raiders - destroy three - to show the Concord you can hold the line.

### [The Long Truce: The Accord](truce_3)
---
scope: shared
state: secret
on_dock: { role: station }
reward: { credits: 800, rep: { iron: { honest: 20, fearsome: 10 } } }
---
Return to a Concord starbase to seal the accord.
